sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/thompson1917-ch09-19> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>;
    dc:description "The polar symmetry of the radial spines in Radiolaria cannot be explained by any obvious mechanical forces of the peripheral froth; it arises in the central living protoplasm, and may reflect obscure but still physical directive forces analogous to Lehmann's 'Gestaltungskraft' in fluid crystals.";
    dc:type "mechanism";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Radiolarian axial polarity arises in the central protoplasm, unexplained by mechanics";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "D’Arcy Wentworth Thompson, On Growth and Form (1st ed., Cambridge: Cambridge University Press, 1917), Chapter IX, “On Concretions, Spicules, and Spicular Skeletons”; topic “Polarity and Lehmann's fluid crystals”. Scope: Radiolaria with fixed numbers and positions of radial spines (Acantharia, Phaeodaria)"
}
